<title>NORWAY: Norway daily gas exports to Europe hit record.</title>
<headline>Norway daily gas exports to Europe hit record.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daily gas exports to continental Europe through pipelines operated by Den norske stats oljeselskap AS (Statoil) topped 100 million cubic metres for the first time on December 23, Statoil's Status Weekly newsletter said.</p>
<p>Statoil said the increased flow through Statpipe, Europipe and Zeepipe reflected the cold winter.</p>
<p>After the giant Troll field began official deliveries on October 1, daily exports have averaged around 95 million cubic metres, the company said.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
